        {
          "question": "e-6653",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sin}\u20613t} & =\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+{3}^{2}}=\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9}} & ={L}^{-1}{L{\\operatorname{sin}\u20613t}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}\u20613t.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
